## Configuration

Call `load_settings()` once at startup, then pass settings to the modules that need
them. It reads environment variables and defaults; files require explicit selection
with `env_file=Path(".env")` or `secrets_dir=Path("/run/secrets")`.
{% if project_type == "cli" %}
```bash
uv run {{ project_slug }} --env-file .env info
```
{% endif %}
Priority is constructor overrides, environment variables, the selected dotenv file,
the selected secret files, then defaults. All relative paths use the working
directory. `.env.example` lists every supported key; secret filenames use the same
nested names. Explicit missing paths fail at startup.

See the [reference](reference.md) for the full API.
